  "limits": [
    "Single dataset; permutation touches pathway labels only, not drug or cell identity.",
    "Retrospective candidate pool; SYNERGY_DELTA_AUC is a model-fitted quantity.",
    "No mechanistic, clinical or drug-choice claim; no meta-learning or RSI."
  ],
  "structural_cause": "the unit key is (cell, combination), so the same compound pair appears in BOTH the training set and the candidate pool under different cells. Any feature that identifies the drug set therefore retains predictive signal, which is why rho stays at 0.24 even with fully permuted pathway labels (tissue-only would be about 0.10)",
  "required_fix": "group split by combination: no compound pair shared between training and the candidate pool",
  "implementation_bugs_fixed_before_results": [
    "first version permuted pathway LEVEL NAMES, which is only a column permutation and leaves ridge unchanged",
    "second version mixed anchor and library roles, raising KeyError for drugs that only appear as library agents",
    "the fix permutes anchor labels among anchor drugs and library labels among library drugs"
  ]
}